; rec76 — COMP+OVD+DELAY combi (type 0x51, Multi "Delay Complex" group).
; PM byte-identical to rec75; the DST->OVD change is pure DATA, and it
; reproduces the dynamics doc's engine-A/engine-B distortion taxonomy inside
; one program:
; - the c028 float LUT = CURVE B (smooth concave knee, slopes 8/2.67/1.67/
;   1/0.67/0.33.../0.083... — rec18's = the GUI Overdrive curve) instead of
;   rec75's curve A;
; - the post-LUT one-pole is ENABLED as a unity-DC tone smoother: k1 = c00e =
;   0.2 (Q31), k2 = PM state 9801 = 0x66666666 = 0.8 -> H = 0.2/(1-0.8z^-1),
;   DC gain exactly 1.0, -3 dB ~1.6 kHz (engine B's "tube rounding" smoother
;   stage, its coefficient hidden in PM state exactly like rec18's).
; Everything else (AGC compressor front, 5000/5000-smp float echo, 0.0625y +
; 0.5*tap output mix) = rec75. See sym/rec75.sym and
; dsp/final-batch-algorithms.md §4.
pm:0x8400  CmpOvd_entry           ; I0 = I1 (all labels = rec75's, one PM)
pm:0x8407  CmpOvd_env             ; family envelope
pm:0x840c  CmpOvd_agcRecip        ; drive = 0.111 + 8.35e8/env clamp 4.0
pm:0x841a  CmpOvd_lutLerpL        ; float lerp of CURVE B
pm:0x841f  CmpOvd_smootherL       ; y = 0.2*shaped + 0.8*y' — ENABLED unity-DC tone smoother
pm:0x8428  CmpOvd_echoL           ; 5000-smp float echo
pm:0x8440  CmpOvd_echoR           ; 5000-smp float echo
pm:0x8447  CmpOvd_outL            ; out = 0.0625y + 0.5*tap, x wet, >>8
pm:0x844b  CmpOvd_outR
dm:0x9801  cmpovd_smoother_k2     ; 0x66666666 = 0.8 Q31 — tone-smoother pole (rec75: 0)
dm:0xc00e  cmpovd_smoother_k1     ; 0x19999999 = 0.2 Q31 — in-gain (unity DC with k2=0.8)
dm:0xc028  cmpovd_curveB          ; 33-pt float LUT: CURVE B smooth knee (rec18's Overdrive curve)
